    {
      "id": "dates",
      "title": "Dates, native first",
      "summary": "NaiveDate and Weekday for the date scenarios, with UTV's CivilDate as the other side.",
      "subject": [
        {
          "path": "implementations/rust/src/typed/.dev/feature.json",
          "entityId": "valid-by-construction"
        },
        {
          "path": "implementations/rust/src/.dev/feature.json",
          "entityId": "month-end"
        }
      ],
      "criteria": [
        "NaiveDate::from_ymd_opt makes 5 November 2026 and -500-03-01, and returns None, with no reason, for 30 February, month 13 and year 275760, which is beyond its range",
        "NaiveDate::MAX is the last day of 262142; NaiveDate's FromStr reads 2026-11-05 and refuses 2026-02-30 as out of range",
        "weekday is Thursday and iso_week 45 for 5 November 2026; leap_year agrees with UTV for every kind of year",
        "Weekday::num_days_from_monday numbers Sunday 6, number_from_monday numbers it 7 like UTV's Weekday",
        "checked_add_days crosses a month end; checked_add_months clamps 31 January + 1 month to 28 February silently; with_month returns None for a missing day",
        "signed_duration_since counts days; < orders dates",
        "and_hms_opt makes a wall-clock date-time and refuses second 60; and_hms_milli_opt writes a leap second as 59 plus 1000 ms"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "automated",
          "path": "implementations/rust/tests/native_first/naive_date.rs",
          "symbol": "from_ymd_opt",
          "command": "cargo test"
        },
